.", "reference": "1640, William Lithgow, “The Sixt Part”, in The Totall Diſcourſe, Of the rare Adventures, and painefull Peregrinations of long nineteene yeares Travailes from Scotland, to the moſt famous Kingdomes in Europe, Aſia, and Affrica […], London: I. Okes, page 249:"}, {"text": "Eternity, before the world and after, is without our reach.", "reference": "c. 1689, Thomas Burnet, The Sacred Theory of the Earth:"}, {"text": "[…] though it was pitch-dark, and we were obliged to be escorted by grooms and groomlings with candles and lanterns; a very necessary precaution, as the winds blew not more violently without the house than within.", "reference": "1835, William Beckford, Italy: With Sketches of Spain and Portugal, volume 1, page 13:"}, {"text": "[...] nor shall any slave holder be allowed to emancipate his or her slave or slaves without the consent of congress, unless he or she shall send his or her slave or slaves without the limits of the republic [of Texas].", "reference": "1838 [1836], “Constitution of the Republic of Texas”, in Laws of the Republic of Texas, in Two Volumes, volume 1, Houston, archived from the original on 08 Jun 2021, Provisions, page 19:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": ["within"], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "Not having, containing, characteristic of, etc.", "tags": [], "examples": ["It was a mistake to leave my house without a coat.", "I was without formal education but was well read and articulate.", "1967, Paul McCartney (writer), The Beatles, Sgt. Pepper's Lonely Hearts Club Band\nLife goes on within you and without you."], "quotes": [{"text": "From another point of view, it was a place without a soul. The well-to-do had hearts of stone; the rich were brutally bumptious; the Press, the Municipality, all the public men, were ridiculously, vaingloriously self-satisfied.", "reference": "1918, W[illiam] B[abington] Maxwell, chapter XXII, in The Mirror and the Lamp, Indianapolis, Ind.: The Bobbs-Merrill Company, →OCLC:"}, {"text": "One day my dreams were surely dying, dying, dying baby\nJust like a flower without rain", "reference": "1968 December 8, Henry Cosby, Sylvia Moy, Stevie Wonder, “I’d Be a Fool Right Now”, in For Once in My Life, performed by Stevie Wonder, Tamla Records:"}, {"text": "Even without hovering drones, a lurking assassin, a thumping score and a denouement, the real-life story of Edward Snowden, a rogue spy on the run, could be straight out of the cinema.", "reference": "2013 June 29, “Travels and travails”, in The Economist, volume 407, number 8842, page 55:"}, {"text": "\"Read lips: Without gas or without you? Without you. Without light or without you? Without you. Without water or without you? Without you. Without food or without you? Without you.\n\"Cold, hunger, darkness and thirst are not as terrible and deadly for us as your \"friendship and brotherhood.\"", "reference": "2022 September 11, Scott McDonald, quoting President Volodymyr Zelensky, “Cold, Hunger and Darkness in Ukraine 'Not as Terrible' as Russia: Zelensky”, in Newsweek, archived from the original on 12 Sep 2022:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": ["with"], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "af", "name": "Afrikaans"}, "word": "sonder"}, {"language": {"code": "sq", "name": "Albanian"}, "word": "pa"}, {"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "بِدُونِ"}, {"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "بِلَا"}, {"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "بِغَيْرِ"}, {"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "دُونَ"}, {"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "مِنْ دُونِ"}, {"language": {"code": "arz", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "من غير"}, {"language": {"code": "acw", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "بِدون"}, {"language": {"code": "acw", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "مِن غير"}, {"language": {"code": "acm", "name": "Iraqi Arabic"}, "word": "ابليا"}, {"language": {"code": "ary", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "بلا"}, {"language": {"code": "